w well it handles corners. Feels stable at high speeds.”\n•\t“The stem is too stiff, transmitting a lot of road buzz to my hands.”\n•\t“Love the matte finish. Looks sleek and doesn’t show fingerprints.”\n•\t“The frame size runs small. Had to size up compared to my previous bike.”\n•\t“The wide rims make for a smoother ride and better aerodynamics.”\n•\t“Disappointed that it doesn’t come with pedals. An extra expense I wasn’t expecting.”\n•\t“The fork is incredibly responsive. Steering is precise and confidence-inspiring.”\n•\t“The seat clamp design makes it difficult to adjust saddle angle.”\n•\t“Impressed with how well it climbs. The low weight really makes a difference.”\n•\t“The brake cables rub against the frame, causing paint wear.”\n•\t“Love the wide range cassette. Makes climbing long steep hills much more manageable.”\n•\t“The headset developed play after just a few months of use.”\n•\t“The aero seatpost design looks great but limits adjustment options.”\n•\t“Fantastic value for money. Performs like bikes twice its price.”\n•\t“Wish it had more color options. The available choices are quite limited.”\n•\t“The frame’s compliance is perfect for long rides on rough roads.”",
            "VersionNumber": 1,
            "UUID": "0c4cf5e3-6258-42dc-8c43-16173135a5c2",
